<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fort Zeelandia (Taiwan)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1624–1662</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fort Zeelandia was the fortress built by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> from 1624 at Tayouan, now Anping in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tainan">Tainan</a>, as the seat of government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> Formosa. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koxinga">Koxinga</a> besieged it in 1661, and in February 1662 its governor, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-coyett">Frederick Coyett</a>, surrendered, ending Dutch rule on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zheng-family">Zheng family</a> of the Kingdom of Tungning then used it as a residence, and parts of its brick walls survive.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fort-zeelandia-taiwan.jpg" alt="Fort Zeelandia (Taiwan)" width="320" height="207" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fort_Zeelandia,_Anping_District,_Tainan_City_(Taiwan).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
